<title>USA: Mosinee sees market conditions akin to '96.</title>
<headline>Mosinee sees market conditions akin to '96.</headline>
<dateline>MOSINEE, Wis. 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mosinee Paper Corp, reporting improved fourth-quarter and full-year 1996 earnings, said it believes market conditions look similar in 1997 to last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Our profit growth in 1997 will come from several factors, which include capacity growth in our Bay West towel and tissue operation and fine funing of our production capabilities at our specialty paper operations,&quot; said president Daniel Olvey in a statement.</p>
<p>Mosinee Paper posted 1996 earnings of $2.56 a share on sales of $314.5 million.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
